      "body": "Quick Answer\n\nTunnel Escape Fates Entwined platforms are Windows 7, 8, 8.1, 10, and 11 only as of the 2026-09-30 research date. The Steam store lists the game as single-player only, with no controller row published. Console support (Switch, PS5, Xbox), macOS, and Linux are not announced as of 2026-09-30. Confirmation of any new platform requires an updated Steam store platform row or developer statement.\n\nTunnel Escape Fates Entwined Platforms — Supported Windows Versions\n\nThe Steam store page for AppID 4285110 lists the supported Windows versions for Tunnel Escape Fates Entwined directly. The SteamDB metadata snapshot confirms the same row on the same date.\n\n| OS family | Supported versions |\n| --- | --- |\n| Windows | Windows 7, Windows 8, Windows 8.1, Windows 10, Windows 11 |\n\nThe supported-OS list is taken from the Steam store Supported Platforms row and is the only confirmed platform scope as of 2026-09-30. There is no minimum-build distinction between Windows 7 and Windows 11 in the store row; both groups report any value from the same entry, and additional 32-bit / 64-bit notes are not announced as of the research date.\n\nSingle-Player Only Restriction\n\nThe Steam store page lists Tunnel Escape Fates Entwined as single-player only. The platform-scope row on the store does not include any co-op, multiplayer, or shared-screen mode, and the SteamDB dated snapshot agrees with the store on the same date.\n\n- Player mode: Single-player only.\n- Online / co-op: Not announced as of 2026-09-30.\n- Local split-screen: Not announced as of 2026-09-30.\n\nIf Elzee or Saikey Studios publishes a multiplayer or split-screen mode after launch, this page should be updated and the platform-scope note refreshed.\n\nNot Announced Platforms\n\nSeveral frequently asked platforms are not announced as of 2026-09-30. These statements will need re-checking once the developer publishes additional information.\n\n- Nintendo Switch — Not announced as of 2026-09-30. The Steam store does not list Switch. Confirmation would require a Nintendo eShop listing or developer statement.\n- PlayStation 5 (PS5) — Not announced as of 2026-09-30. The Steam store does not list PS5. Confirmation would require a PlayStation Store listing or developer statement.\n- Xbox Series X / S (and Xbox One) — Not announced as of 2026-09-30. The Steam store does not list Xbox. Confirmation would require an Xbox Store listing or developer statement.\n- macOS — Not announced as of 2026-09-30. The Steam store does not list macOS. Confirmation would require a macOS row on the Steam platform list or an official Mac App Store / Steam macOS listing.\n- Linux / SteamOS + Proton — Not announced as of 2026-09-30. The Steam store does not list Linux. Confirmation would require a SteamOS + Linux row on the Steam platform list or a developer statement.\n\nController support notes and Steam Deck verification status are also not announced as of 2026-09-30 and would require a Steam store controller row or a Steam Deck Verified / Playable badge before they could be listed here."
